MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "City of Evil feels like a natural next choice because its fast riffs, melodic hooks, and elaborate guitar work connect with what draws me to Advance And Vanquish and In Flames.",
    "Death Magnetic and Hypnotize fit my appetite for heavier music: one offers aggressive riffs, while the other adds the unusual rhythms and structures that appeal to me in Disturbed and Tool."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "X&Y and How to Dismantle An Atomic feel too soft for what I want now; sharing a broad rock sound with some of my past listening does not give them the intensity I am seeking.",
    "Fallen, Halestorm, Chapter V, and Daughtry connect with parts of my taste, but that familiarity is not enough to make me choose them ahead of more energetic metal today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in The Reason and One Day Remains seems to have been taken as a broad desire for melodic rock, even when the recommendations lack the heavier edge I currently want.",
    "An apparent connection to Tool makes Operation: Mindcrime II understandable, but progressive complexity alone does not make me ready to choose a sequel album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated In Flames listening and interest in Advance And Vanquish suggest that the combination of heaviness, speed, and melody matters more than simply sounding like rock.",
    "My latest choices, Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days, make forceful rhythms and adventurous song structures especially relevant to what I want next."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my rock and metal interests, but only some capture the energetic heaviness and musical complexity I want right now."
}
